------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party material redistributed in every compiled .pikelet pack
------------------------------------------------------------------------

`pikelet compile` embeds a query encoder in each pack it writes, and the
pikelet package downloads the same encoder on first use. A pack therefore
redistributes the following, each under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(the same license as Pikelet; see LICENSE):

all-MiniLM-L6-v2
  Model weights from sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2
  (https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2),
  licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  Modified: the weights are quantized to 8-bit integers in blocks of 64
  and repacked into Pikelet's encoder blob format. Packs compiled with
  --encoder-model carry that model instead, under its own license.

BERT WordPiece vocabulary
  vocab.txt from bert-base-uncased (https://github.com/google-research/bert,
  https://huggingface.co/google-bert/bert-base-uncased), Copyright Google,
  licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Redistributed unmodified.

The content a pack is compiled from is the compiler's user's, under
whatever license they record with --license.
